Description: two-pane Markdown viewer and editor built with Qt Widgets
 Total Markdown opens a Markdown document in two panes: the source, syntax
 highlighted, on the left and the rendered preview on the right, both kept in
 step while you type. It is built on Qt Widgets only — no web engine — which
 keeps the startup instant and the rendering fully native.
 .
 Documents support CommonMark and GitHub Flavored Markdown (tables, task
 lists, strikethrough, autolinks), fenced code blocks highlighted per language
 by KDE's KSyntaxHighlighting, LaTeX formulas typeset by the bundled MicroTeX
 engine, images resolved relative to the document, remote images downloaded in
 the background and cached on disk, and animated GIF and SVG badges.
